&lt;h2&gt;Role purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of AI and Technology is accountable for the direction, delivery and adoption of AI across Teneo Management Consulting and for ensuring that its broader technology environment supports the needs of the business. The role sets the AI strategy and investment priorities, leads the AI Engineering team, owns the strategy and priorities for Management Consulting-specific technology, software, data, knowledge-management workflows and subscriptions, and acts as the principal Management Consulting stakeholder for Teneo IT on centrally managed technology, data platforms and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role connects Management Consulting&#39;s priorities with Teneo&#39;s central AI team, Teneo IT and other control and enabling functions. It translates business needs into Management Consulting-owned AI and technology initiatives or clear requirements for central teams, moves high-value AI and software solutions from experimentation into reliable use, and gives consultants the skills and support required to use approved AI tools effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is primarily an internal capability role. The role is accountable for the allocation and utilisation of the AI Engineering team, including support for selected client engagements, and for the Management Consulting-specific AI and broader technology within its remit. Teneo IT and Teneo&#39;s central AI team remain accountable for the centrally managed services and capabilities, while Management Consulting engagement leaders retain accountability for client relationships, overall engagement delivery and revenue targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AI strategy and priorities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Management Consulting AI strategy, roadmap and priorities, aligned with the business strategy and Teneo-wide AI direction. Consult Teneo&#39;s central AI team on new solutions to reuse firm-wide capabilities, avoid duplication and manage enterprise dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and assess AI opportunities across consulting delivery, business development, proposition development, internal operations and knowledge work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own prioritisation of AI opportunities and allocation of AI Engineering capacity within the approved budget, considering value, feasibility, risk, reuse potential, capacity and cost. Escalate material investments, major reprioritisation and strategically sensitive work to Management Consulting leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop business cases and recommend whether Management Consulting should build, buy, partner, reuse a central capability, scale an existing initiative or stop further investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define outcome measures for priority AI initiatives and report progress, realised value, adoption, spend, risks and dependencies to Management Consulting and wider Teneo leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership of the AI Engineering team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the day-to-day work of the Management Consulting AI Engineering team, including objectives, prioritisation, resource allocation, workforce planning, utilisation, delivery oversight and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance the team&#39;s capacity across client engagements, internal tooling development, enablement of the broader MC team, and technical capability improvement, while maintaining sustainable workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce engineering and product standards for Management Consulting AI solutions, consistent with mandatory Teneo-wide architecture, AI, security and technology standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define clear demand, resourcing and decision-making processes between the AI Engineering team and key stakeholders, including Resourcing, Operations, Finance, project leads and the wider client-facing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the team&#39;s capability through recruitment, coaching, feedback, career development and targeted use of external partners where justified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high practical AI fluency and sufficient technical understanding to create simple prototypes, automations and demonstrations, evaluate their outputs and translate business needs into clear engineering requirements, without becoming the bottleneck for implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;AI service lifecycle&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the path from discovery and prototyping to production, adoption, support and retirement for Management Consulting AI solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure solutions are designed for reuse where appropriate and integrate with approved data, identity, security and collaboration environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish proportionate evaluation and monitoring for quality, reliability, user experience, cost and risk, including controls for generative AI outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define ownership and support arrangements before launch, and ensure that technical debt, maintenance and business continuity inform investment and prioritisation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Business partnership and consulting integration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Management Consulting leadership and practice leads to translate business priorities into a focused AI agenda and secure decisions on investment, risk and operating change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support proposition and methodology development by identifying where approved AI capabilities can improve the quality, speed or differentiation of consulting work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise case teams on feasible and responsible use of AI, deploying the AI Engineering team where specialist support is justified. Own the team&#39;s allocation and utilisation; engagement leaders remain accountable for client relationships and engagement delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Management Consulting in relevant Teneo forums and maintain productive relationships with external technology and delivery partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Teneo IT partnership and centrally managed technology&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the principal Management Consulting stakeholder for Teneo IT, representing the business&#39;s needs and priorities in relation to centrally managed technology, data platforms and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Management Consulting requirements into clear input for firm-wide technology strategy, roadmaps and investment decisions, and communicate central plans, constraints and decisions to Management Consulting leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Teneo IT and relevant central functions on architecture, integration, identity and access, hosting, resilience, service support and technology changes affecting Management Consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the performance of centrally managed services within Management Consulting, escalating material issues and working with Teneo IT to agree appropriate action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Management Consulting technology, knowledge management and subscriptions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy, roadmap and priorities for Management Consulting-specific technology, software, data and subscriptions, aligned with business and AI priorities and Teneo-wide standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a coherent view of Management Consulting applications, data sources, knowledge assets, licences and subscriptions, reducing duplication and addressing material capability gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own selected technology-enabled knowledge-management workflows, including the capture, organisation, permissioning, retrieval and reuse of knowledge for consulting and AI-enabled workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with client-facing teams and designated knowledge owners to establish clear accountability for the quality, permissions and appropriate use of knowledge assets, while acting as a key stakeholder in wider knowledge-management decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead business cases, supplier evaluation, procurement and renewals for Management Consulting-specific tools and services. Manage approved expenditure, licences and consumption within delegated authority and the relevant central approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Training enablement and adoption&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the AI capability-building plan for Management Consulting, based on the needs of different roles, practices and levels of experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct practical training, guidance, demonstrations, office hours and communities of practice that help colleagues apply approved tools to real consulting workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand the network of leaders and super-users who can reinforce good practice, surface demand and support adoption within their teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure confidence, active use, quality and workflow impact, and adapt the enablement programme where training does not translate into sustained behaviour change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear communication on available tools, expected use, limitations, new releases and routes for support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsible AI governance and risk&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult Teneo&#39;s central AI team on proposed solutions to identify existing capabilities, avoid duplication and maintain alignment with Teneo-wide AI direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Cyber Security, Risk, Legal and IT to translate firm-wide requirements into practical delivery and usage controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure new AI solutions receive the required Cyber Security and Risk approvals prior to implementation, with clear records of decisions, exceptions and accountable owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote safe handling of client and firm information and address emerging model, vendor and regulatory risks as the technology changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience and capabilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience setting and delivering an AI and technology strategy in a professional services, consulting or similarly knowledge-intensive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience leading multidisciplinary technical teams and taking AI or software products from discovery into secure, supported production use, with the judgement to challenge decisions on architecture, integration, evaluation, security and operational support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High practical AI fluency, demonstrated through regular use of generative AI tools and the ability to create and evaluate simple prototypes, automations or workflows. Production coding experience is not required, but the candidate must recognise when specialist engineering support is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of converting ambiguous business needs into prioritised initiatives, investment cases, delivery plans and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of technology and data governance, including responsible AI, information security, privacy, vendor risk and approval processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving data or knowledge-management workflows in a professional services or similarly knowledge-intensive environment, particularly where these support enterprise search, knowledge retrieval or AI-enabled use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial judgement in build-versus-buy decisions, vendor selection, budgets, licences, subscriptions and consumption management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing enablement or change programmes that produce sustained adoption, rather than training attendance alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a business unit in relation to centrally managed technology services, translating requirements, explaining technical choices clearly and influencing enterprise technology priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leader: sets direction, develops talent, gives clear feedback and builds effective teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Level Up Your Career with Zynga!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zynga, we bring people together through the power of play. As a global leader in interactive entertainment and a proud label of Take-Two Interactive, our games have been downloaded over 6 billion times—connecting players in 175+ countries through fun, strategy, and a little friendly competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From thrilling casino spins to epic strategy battles, mind-bending puzzles, and social word challenges, our diverse game portfolio has something for everyone. Fan-favorites and latest hits include FarmVille™, Words With Friends™, Zynga Poker™, Game of Thrones Slots Casino™, Wizard of Oz Slots™, Hit it Rich! Slots™, Wonka Slots™, Top Eleven™, Toon Blast™, Empires &amp;amp; Puzzles™, Merge Dragons!™, CSR Racing™, Harry Potter: Puzzles &amp;amp; Spells™, Match Factory™, and Color Block Jam™—plus many more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007 and headquartered in California, our teams span North America, Europe, and Asia, working together to craft unforgettable gaming experiences. Whether you&#39;re spinning, strategizing, matching, or competing, Zynga is where fun meets innovation—and where you can take your career to the next level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be part of the play!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At NaturalMotion, we make games that wow people. We innovate to create previously impossible experiences that would not exist without us. We take pride in making titles that reach a large audience and creating communities that last. Our commitment to excellence has earned us recognition as one of the UK&#39;s Best Places to Work in games for eight consecutive years by gamesindustry.biz, and we&#39;re proud to be part of the Zynga and Take-Two Interactive family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Server &amp;amp; Infrastructure Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our server engineering team. In this role, you will work on core backend systems and backend services, contributing directly to live services and build systems with minimal supervision. You will help manage and expand our infrastructure, automated CI/CD pipelines, and development tools while collaborating closely with technical leads to build reliable, high-performing server environments. You will have a passion for large-scale high-availability systems, a devotion to software craftsmanship, an unwavering commitment to quality, and the desire to have their work seen by tens of millions of people worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Server &amp;amp; Infrastructure Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Complete multi-day backend engineering tasks with minimal guidance. Design, deploy, and support scalable server architectures and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps &amp;amp; Pipeline Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Build, maintain, and optimise robust CI/CD workflows and automated deployment pipelines across cloud environments and build platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in technical planning, architectural brainstorming, and technical cost/complexity estimation for multi-week efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Efficiency &amp;amp; Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify workflow bottlenecks and drive initiatives to improve overall engineering team productivity, tooling, and code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in internal tech talks, share best practices, and maintain collaborative peer relationships across engineering squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Python, Go and C#&lt;/strong&gt; for backend services, automation scripts, and custom tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Infrastructure &amp;amp; IaC:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience provisioning and managing &lt;strong&gt;AWS&lt;/strong&gt; infrastructure using &lt;strong&gt;Terraform&lt;/strong&gt; (Infrastructure as Code).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Platform Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience configuring and managing automated orchestration/build platforms (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Unreal Horde&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Jenkins&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;TeamCity&lt;/strong&gt;), preferably with &lt;strong&gt;Game Engines (Unreal Engine, Unity, etc.)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source Control Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of version control systems and workflow strategies (&lt;strong&gt;GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Perforce/Helix Core&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Git-flow&lt;/strong&gt;, branch management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage moderate-to-complex technical tasks independently, break down project deliverables, and communicate status accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing server-side logic and managing database dependencies for live applications or multiplayer services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked in, or has a strong interest in the gaming industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in infrastructure deployment and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in mentoring junior team members or interns, framing task deconstruction, and conducting technical interviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerisation (&lt;strong&gt;Docker, Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;) and infrastructure security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and discretionary annual bonus scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days holiday, plus bank holidays &amp;amp; 2 paid personal days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 months fully paid maternity/adoption leave and 16 weeks fully paid paternity leave (eligibility criteria applies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan, with a double matching employer contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical &amp;amp; dental insurance and healthcare cash plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life insurance, personal accident insurance and income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and neurodiversity support programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Employee Stock Purchase Plan (eligibility criteria applies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fitness reimbursement plan, worth £600 per annum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly happy hours, seasonal parties and monthly social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual rail season ticket advance and cycle to work scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer, which means we are committed to creating and celebrating diverse thoughts, cultures, and backgrounds throughout our organization.&amp;nbsp; Employment with us is based on substantive ability, objective qualifications, and work ethic – not an individual’s race, creed, color, religion, sex or gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin or ancestry, alienage or citizenship status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, status as a victim of domestic violence or sex offenses, reproductive health decision, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, we are committed to providing the necessary support and accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities, health conditions, or impairments (subject to any local qualifying requirements) to ensure their full participation in the job application or interview process. Please contact us at ----- to request any accommodations or for support related to your application for an open position.&lt;/p&gt;
